# The build context is the repository root, and everything here is either
# rebuilt inside the image, useless to it, or must never be in it.

# Rebuilt in the image. Copying a host `node_modules` would also copy whatever
# platform-specific binaries the developer's machine installed.
node_modules
**/node_modules
apps/*/dist
apps/*/coverage
packages/*/dist
.turbo
**/.turbo
**/.vite

# Secrets. `config/` is the *running* deployment's folder — it holds real
# connection strings — and `config.example/` is the one that ships (CFG-1).
# Getting these two the wrong way round would bake an operator's credentials
# into a published image.
config/
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# The deployment artefacts themselves (D51). The Dockerfile is passed to the
# builder by path and never read out of the context, and the compose file and
# the `idp-*` scripts are how you *run* the image rather than anything it needs.
docker/

# History and tooling that the image has no use for.
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
.claude
.agents
docs
audits
*.md
!README.md

# Test and local artefacts.
playwright-report
test-results
coverage
*.log
